        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "Two congruent regular tetrahedra, each of edge length \\(a\\), are joined along one common triangular face. Find the volume of the resulting solid.",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The volume of one regular tetrahedron is \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\times\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}a^2\\times\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}a=\\frac{a^3}{6\\sqrt{2}}\\). Hence, the combined volume is \\(2\\times\\frac{a^3}{6\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{a^3}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 119,
