        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "A cube of edge length \\(a\\) has a square pyramid of height \\(h\\) attached to one of its square faces. The pyramid has the same base as that face and slant height \\(l\\). Find the total external surface area of the composite solid.",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The attached cube face becomes internal, so the cube contributes \\(5a^2\\). The four triangular faces of the pyramid contribute \\(4\\times\\frac{1}{2}al=2al\\). Therefore, the total external area is \\(5a^2+2al\\).",
